<h2>Measured</h2>
<p>Measured combines incrementality testing, MMM, and media optimization with an emphasis on causal experiments.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Brands that want test-calibrated measurement and ongoing media optimization.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Enterprise custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Recast:</strong> Measured emphasizes incrementality testing as the core workflow; Recast emphasizes Bayesian MMM and uncertainty-aware modeling.</p>
<p><a href="/measured">Learn more about Measured on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>Keen</h2>
<p>Keen helps marketers plan, forecast, and optimize budget allocation across marketing investments.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Leadership teams that need budget scenarios and investment planning.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Enterprise custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Recast:</strong> Keen is more decision and planning oriented; Recast is more statistically centered around MMM rigor.</p>
<p><a href="/keen">Learn more about Keen on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>Rockerbox</h2>
<p>Rockerbox provides attribution and marketing measurement workflows for performance teams.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Teams that need campaign, channel, and customer journey reporting.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Recast:</strong> More attribution-oriented and operational; less focused on Bayesian MMM.</p>

<h2>Northbeam</h2>
<p>Northbeam is an attribution and optimization platform used by ecommerce and DTC advertisers.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Ecommerce teams making frequent budget decisions across paid media channels.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Mid-market to enterprise depending on spend and scope.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Recast:</strong> More dashboard and attribution workflow oriented; Recast is stronger for model-based budget planning.</p>
<p><a href="/northbeam">Learn more about Northbeam on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>Haus</h2>
<p>Haus focuses on incrementality experiments and causal measurement for marketing teams.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Brands that want controlled testing and decision support.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Recast:</strong> More experiment-led; Recast is more MMM-led with incrementality calibration.</p>

<h2>Nielsen MMM</h2>
<p>Nielsen offers enterprise marketing mix modeling and measurement services for large advertisers.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Large brands that want measurement services within the Nielsen ecosystem.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Enterprise custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Recast:</strong> More services and enterprise data ecosystem; Recast is a specialized MMM platform.</p>

<h2>How to Choose</h2>
<p>Choose Recast for Bayesian MMM and uncertainty-aware planning. Choose Measured or Haus for incrementality-led workflows, Keen for investment planning, Rockerbox or Northbeam for attribution operations, and Nielsen MMM for enterprise services.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>What is the closest Recast alternative?</h3>
<p>Measured is close for MMM plus incrementality, while Nielsen MMM is close for enterprise marketing mix modeling services.</p>
<h3>Which alternative is best for incrementality testing?</h3>
<p>Measured and Haus are the strongest incrementality-focused alternatives in this set.</p>
<h3>Which alternative is best for ecommerce?</h3>
<p>Northbeam is often better aligned with ecommerce and DTC operating workflows.</p>
<h3>Do Recast alternatives publish pricing?</h3>
<p>Most MMM and incrementality vendors are custom-quoted. Attribution-focused tools may provide more pricing guidance, but scope still matters.</p>
<h3>Is attribution a replacement for MMM?</h3>
<p>No. Attribution and MMM answer different questions. Attribution helps explain touchpoint paths, while MMM estimates channel contribution and budget response at an aggregate level.</p>

